{
 "_about": "Seed of the ESC database for the Express wizard (Malcolm 2026-09-05 '… and the ESC!'). 'Which ESC?' → Rotorflight ESC telemetry protocol, wiring, half-duplex, ESC-side settings (governor OFF/external — Rotorflight's governor drives the head speed), forward programming from the phone. Protocol names as Rotorflight 2.x shows them. Sources per entry; verified=true when read from Rotorflight docs or the ESC maker.",
 "_rule": "Every entry: ESC governor OFF / external, throttle range calibrated, ESC telemetry wire (ESC TX → FC UART RX) unless noted. Rotorflight needs motor poles + gear ratio for RPM.",
 "_not_listed": "Ask: does it have a telemetry wire? (no → protocol NONE, RPM from a sensor or none) — then 'set its governor to OFF / external and calibrate the throttle'.",
